update backend to only use postgres  [DONE]
   X - views.py rewritten for postgres only (login, register, save_team)
   X - users + teams tables created, get_user_profile() function in place
   X - keep all hand-written SQL (tables, functions) in backend/sql/ so it lives in git
   X - make sure /saveteam reads the user from the token, not the request body

remove mongo from everywhere
   X - backend: remove pymongo from requirements.txt, MONGO_URI from .env, MONGO_* from settings.py
   X - frontend: npm uninstall mongoose pg express cors dotenv jsonwebtoken body-parser bcryptjs
   X - frontend: remove the "start": "node ../API/server.js" script from package.json
   X - userStore.js: mongo_id -> id everywhere
   X - userStore.js: saveTeam sends "Authorization: Bearer <token>" header, no id in body
   X - userStore.js: fix logout (clears id but should clear token too)

security + cleanup (before going live)
    - set real DJANGO_SECRET_KEY and JWT_SECRET in .env (not the defaults)
    - set ALLOWED_HOSTS in production
